$image2text — vision-language (Qwen2-VL)

SUMMARY
  Runs Qwen2-VL on each images[] file with a prompt and writes model text into texts[]
  (one .txt per image).

SYNTAX
  $image2text
  $image2text(gpu=True)
  $image2text(max_tokens=256)
  $image2text(prompt='What bird is this?')

INPUT
  images[]  — source images (PNG, JPG, …)
  prompts[] — optional per-image questions (or instruction body / prompt= arg)

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one text file per image (model response)

ARGUMENTS
  prompt=     — same prompt for every image (overrides prompts[])
  max_tokens= — generation limit (default 512)
  gpu=        — use CUDA when true (default CPU; or AH_IMAGE2TEXT_GPU=1)

MODELS
  Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct under models/qwen-vl/Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct/
  First run downloads automatically (~4 GB).

DEPENDENCIES
  Uses .venvs/media (torch + transformers). Run tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1 once.
  Or: uv sync --extra media

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE2TEXT=1 — placeholder text, no model load.
  AH_IMAGE2TEXT_GPU=1       — default gpu=True when arg omitted.

EXAMPLE
  @photo: $file('garden.jpg') -> $image2text
  What species of bird is in this photo?

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared on output; images[] pass through; input texts[] replaced.
